WEBVTT

NOTE Miles For Smiles correctional dental care overview (edited cut).

1
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.470 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>Going to correctional facilities,

2
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:14.760 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>what we're really providing is access
to care to a population of people,

3
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.380 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>detained, incarcerated
for whatever reason,

4
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.460 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>but they're still human,
they still have pain,

5
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.850 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>and if we can do something to help
them, that's what we want to do,

6
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.850 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>and so that's kind of how our mobile,
our correctional care started.

7
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.850 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>Miles For Smiles provides
dental care to our inmates.

8
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.550 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>We have a population of
almost 1,500 inmates.

9
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.770 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>The convenience is that they
come here, it's done quickly,

10
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.670 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>so the inmates are seen faster.

11
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.220 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>They don't have to be sent out
to another office to be seen,

12
00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.710 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>they get their dental work right here.

13
00:00:46.202 --> 00:00:48.552 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>The inmates like that
they're seen quicker.

14
00:00:48.602 --> 00:00:51.422 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>They've seen that as soon
as they say a problem,

15
00:00:51.472 --> 00:00:53.192 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>their service is done right then.

16
00:00:53.242 --> 00:00:55.772 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>They're getting x-rayed, they're
getting that tooth pulled or filled,

17
00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:56.612 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>and it's done.

18
00:00:56.662 --> 00:01:01.122 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>There are a lot of inmates
who are requesting dental care

19
00:01:01.172 --> 00:01:03.912 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>and have been for quite some time.

20
00:01:03.962 --> 00:01:05.212 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>We're talking months,

21
00:01:05.262 --> 00:01:09.892 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>so just imagine being confined or
incarcerated for whatever reason and being

22
00:01:09.942 --> 00:01:12.602 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>in pain for months at a time.

23
00:01:12.885 --> 00:01:13.715 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>If they didn't come,

24
00:01:13.765 --> 00:01:16.055 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>then that means that nurses would
have to go out and see these inmates,

25
00:01:16.105 --> 00:01:18.735 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>give them some pain medicine,
see what their problem is,

26
00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:21.115 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>and then probably send them
to a different facility

27
00:01:21.165 --> 00:01:23.695 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>or get their dental work done
so that they're not constantly

28
00:01:23.745 --> 00:01:27.285 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>in pain from that toothache.

29
00:01:30.035 --> 00:01:33.475 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>When we come in, we try to
service up to 20 inmates a day,

30
00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:36.045 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>and we try to do it
within a two-day visit,

31
00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:39.235 line:-6
<v Dr. Jeremy Alexander>so we're servicing about
40 inmates a month.

32
00:01:39.285 --> 00:01:40.915 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>So I want to say thank you
to Miles For Smiles

33
00:01:40.965 --> 00:01:43.305 line:-6
<v Ashley Lanier>for coming to us and
servicing our population.
